  - calibration
  - distribution shift
  - subgroup evaluation
  - health equity
abstract: >
  ASAC is a conceptual and methodological framework for auditing and evaluating
  the reliability of malaria diagnostic artificial intelligence across patient
  subgroups, healthcare sites, image-acquisition conditions, and deployment
  environments. This software provides a minimal reference implementation for
  subgroup performance and calibration auditing. It is intended for research
  and methodological development and is not clinically validated.
